  "items": [
    {
      "id": "I85-01",
      "item": "All six original C2/Hessian/scale assumptions and finite-dimensional real Borel phase including rank0 must be retained in any actual construction consumer.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-01"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-02",
      "item": "Literal Phi/S/rate and iidExp1 initialized stopped recursion A.1-A.2 with sourceE_(n+1)/zero-index adapter, R0=I, infinite waits, half-open arcs, finite stored records and last-live arc.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-02",
        "G85-03",
        "G85-04",
        "G85-10"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-03",
      "item": "Joint measurable source-terminal construction and ASTIS actual all finite time adapter need fixed-parameter AE initialization/arc validity, not uniform-parameter AE or arbitrary correlated states.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-04",
        "G85-10"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-04",
      "item": "Prospective actual law object K(y,r,z,t;A)=P{omega:Z(y,r,z,t,omega) in A}, full phase event A; time remains finite NNReal.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-07",
        "G85-08"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-05",
      "item": "Joint y/reference/initialphase/time kernel measurability follows joint actual phase and actual P probability; these must be derived from actual parent, never supplied as arbitrary phase/measurability premise.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-05",
        "G85-06",
        "G85-07"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-06",
      "item": "K has probability fibers for all inputs; kernel IsMarkovKernel here means total mass1, not process Markov/restart or semigroup.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-09",
        "G85-21"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-07",
      "item": "Actual fixed-parameter AE Z0=z gives K0=dirac z, including exceptional raw clock fallback and rank0; no all-sample identity required.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-10",
        "G85-11"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-08",
      "item": "Bounded Borel test integration under K should equal actual clock expectation, ensuring exported law serves source transition operators rather than only restating measurable pushforward.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-12",
        "G85-13"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-09",
      "item": "Exact q_y and nu_y=q_y x standardGaussian define future initial stationary candidate law; normalization is separate from stationarity.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-14"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-10",
      "item": "Source p4.2-p5.3 path expansion/reversal leads to bounded test identity, takingF=1 gives actual invariance; kernel law interface can give a common typed target for this missing law equality, but cannot prove it.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-15",
        "G85-16"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-11",
      "item": "Source p6.1 invariance+Jensen gives contraction and supports AE-representative semantics; kernel existence alone does not.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-17"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-12",
      "item": "Source p6.2 compact-test bounded DCT is addressed separately; fullallL2 extension additionally requires true contraction/operator and independent C_c density.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-18",
        "G85-19",
        "G85-20"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-13",
      "item": "Source H_y integrates randomreference+Gaussianmomentum at terminal pi and returns position. It is distinct from fullphase K_t with deterministicreference and arbitraryinitialphase/time.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-07"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-14",
      "item": "Literal source uses C_c in boundedtest argument; ASTIS C_b extension must not be relabelled allL2. Kernelevent measurability naturally includes bounded Borel tests independent of that continuity subclass.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-12",
        "G85-19"
      ],
      "coverage": "MAPPED_OR_EXPLICIT_OPEN_BOUNDARY"
    },
    {
      "id": "I85-15",
      "item": "Memorylessness/restart/Markov/timehomogeneity/ChapmanKolmogorov/semigroup/pathreversal/invariance/hypocoercivity/cost/main/composition stay OPEN.",
      "graph_nodes": [
        "G85-15",
        "G85-16",
        "G85-17",
        "G85-18",
        "G85-20",
        "G85-21"
      ],
